<title>JORDAN: Jordan buys 50,000 T U.S. yellow corn.</title>
<headline>Jordan buys 50,000 T U.S. yellow corn.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jordan bought 50,000 tonnes of U.S. No.3 corn in one lot at $141.85 per tonne C and F, for second half December shipment under the GSM 102 programme, traders said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Jordan's Ministry of Supply made the purchase from Geneva based Romak, traders said.</p>
<p>Jordan has an annual consumption of yellow corn of 400,000 to 500,000 tonnes. --Amman Bureau 9626+623776</p>
